hing that  because you don't have any experience  you're going to make a ton of mistakes  and lose everything and i don't want  that for you the better path  is to go find a company that has 10  employees not a huge company but a  smaller company  who's built up to a certain size is a  company you respect and look up to  and where you can learn from and take a  job  it could be an internship it could be a  part-time job it could be a volunteer  paid unpaid whatever it is  there's a few reasons why it's so  important okay the first one is  to see if this is even something that  you want to do  a lot of times you get ideas i get ideas  i'm going to try this out i have this  vision for this thing i want to create  and then you start into something  and it's not what you thought it was you  know you may get into it you may say i  want to make dresses i love dresses  i'm going to start into the dress  business you'll get this job at a dress  company and realize wow this is a  i hate this industry i don't want to be  here  and so that saves you a lot of grief and  agony because you figure that out  working for somebody else instead of  working  you know for yourself and losing a ton  of money and time on it so that's the  first thing it does the second thing is  it teaches you  about the industry it teaches you so  that you don't make mistakes  it teaches you so that when you're ready  to go and launch your own business you  have contacts you have experience you  know what you're doing  like if you went to university right you  paid to go to university you pay to go  to college  here you're either volunteering your  times you're not paying anything  or you're getting paid maybe not a lot  but a little bit you're getting paid to  learn  right university you have to work you  have to work hard right to get your  grades  you're gonna have to work hard at this  company but you're working to learn  and it's cheaper than a university  education so that when you are ready to  go  do your own business you know what  you're doing you've already made your  mistakes  the reason why it's important started a  small company not not the biggest  companies in the field  is because there's lots of opportunities  to learn  in a smaller company right at a big  company you do an unpaid internship you  might be doing a lot of photocopying  getting coffee for people you're not  learning right it may be something  that's great for your resume to say hey  i worked at this huge company  but if your eventual goal is to start  your own business your resume doesn't  matter  you want to learn so a smaller company  10 15 employees  if you can get close to the entrepreneur  they need help  entrepreneurs we need help okay  entrepreneurs never say oh i've got too  much time on my hands right there's  always so much on the go  that you might be hired or brought on  board as a free intern to do one  specific thing  you'll almost always find if you can get  close to the entrepreneur there'll be  more opportunities that open up  entrepreneurs love seeing hard-working  people there  there there aren't too many  entrepreneurs who say yeah all of my  team they're highly motivated they're  super hard working i love all of them  they're they're all fantastic  right there's always there's always room  for great employees for great workers at  companies  so if they see that you're doing a great  job they're going to give you more and  more and more and more and you want that  even if you're not getting paid because  you're  the education is what you're paying for  right your goal isn't to be there  working for free for the next 20 years  your goal is to learn about the business  and then go do your own thing  right if you need more time there they  may they may find that you are  you know your goals will be  indispensable to them and they may offer  you a job and they may give you raises  and you have to decide okay well do i  am i still learning here do i want to  take this 